# Pinned 2026-10-02 by panel 187's compiler engineer, route (1f): a known
# cost, not an intent; a change in either direction turns this case red.
# A head that refused something drops the rest of its line as debris
# (`parse/opening.hero:147`), a stray closer in it with it. Shape `g4/ti`:
# the `)` after the condition is told only once the operand is written.
# Class (b): `adjacent`.
#
# Moved 2026-10-04 with defect 199's repair (lane b9-recovery): the stray `)`
# is told in the same run, `expected_end_of_line`, as past a failed statement
# (`parse/brace_habit.drop_told`); it pins that now, one message a mistake.

function f(a: i64) -> i64
    return a

function main()
    if f(1 +) )  #~ expected_expression expected_end_of_line
        print(1)
